From 98f1ef8f9449577006856b3f593f04dc04b2b620 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:59:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] fix(#95): cut_reasons, collection_conflicts and
 routing_error are read from the types that declare them

The defect, verbatim from the issue: "If a producer renames or stops setting one, the read silently
becomes 'clean'." Thirteen sites read these three with a default of `()` / `""`: "nothing refused this
measurement". A renamed `cut_reasons` on a ConvergeResult or SuiteAudit would have let an ungateable
measurement print a verdict; a renamed `routing_error` would have stripped the evidence the
`routing_failed` remedy acts on.

Why the obvious fix is wrong: the readers hold a ConvergeResult (`result`), a SuiteAudit (`a`) or a
SurvivorReport (`report`, `survivor_report`), each of which declares the field, so those read DIRECTLY.
`validity_cut_reasons` is a ConvergeResult property that is always a tuple, so the two sites that chose
between it and `cut_reasons` read it alone. The one genuinely three-valued source is a PROFILE's stashed
`routing_error`: `profile` sets it after routing and a cache hit returns before that, so ABSENT there
means "routing did not run this session", and a run whose routing failed is cut and never stored.
`_routing_evidence` now takes the profiles and the report apart, reads the profiles with `reading()`,
and handles ABSENT by name (contributes nothing) with the reason written beside it.

Converted: converge._converge_impl, converge._routing_evidence, audit.audit_suite, and cli
_final_banner_status, _format_converge, _floor_caused, _converge_decision, _converge_action,
_audit_measurement_block. Test doubles of ConvergeResult and SuiteAudit gain the fields.

Not closed: `failing_tests` on the engine's profile, and the remaining flag families.

FAULT_OPEN: cut_reasons 6 -> 0, routing_error 4 -> 0, collection_conflicts 3 -> 0; failing_tests 5 -> 4
(its audit site shared this function). Disarmed, 4 of 4 new intent tests fail. The 32-file neighbour
set (673 tests) and the four guards pass under 3.14 and 3.12; ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
